From: scada <scada@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:04:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 52/80] Input: fpc1020: return the gpiod error from the irq
 attribute

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0144VMKxYe33NKa3LLPZNivr
---
 drivers/input/fingerprint/fpc1020_platform.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/fingerprint/fpc1020_platform.c b/drivers/input/fingerprint/fpc1020_platform.c
index e1cd7d4983ac..c82526b0aee1 100644
--- a/drivers/input/fingerprint/fpc1020_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/input/fingerprint/fpc1020_platform.c
@@ -400,6 +400,8 @@ static ssize_t irq_get(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
 	int level;
 
 	level = gpiod_get_value(fpc->irq_gpiod);
+	if (level < 0)
+		return level;
 
 	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%d\n", level);
 }
